{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-83",
  "title": "Thoughts (2)",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Thoughts (2)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**biggest strengths so far:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "you're treating this like a film, not just a website. the “midnight light” concept, the pacing, the cinematic interactions—it all aligns with how he sees the world."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "“expressionist luminescence” as a visual philosophy? yeah, that tracks. his admiration for robert richardson + chris seager, the interplay of darkness and light, the whole sculpting-with-illumination thing—it’s not just about aesthetics, it’s about the way he builds narrative through cinematography."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "the branding feels both old-world and modern. you’re not just dumping “vintage” elements in for the sake of it; you’re weaving them in with intent."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**things to fine-tune:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**balance in the aesthetic**—midnight blue is a solid foundation, but it could get visually heavy. making sure warm “hot accents” aren’t just occasional highlights but play a *functional* role in guiding the eye will be key."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**tone of voice**—his brand shouldn’t be *too* polished or overly lofty. he’s an artist, but he’s also hands-on, technical, and in the trenches of filmmaking. find a balance between cinematic grandeur and the real-world grind of camera work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**interactivity**—the “before/after lighting toggle” is a great idea, but don't make it a gimmick. ensure every interactive element adds something *felt*, not just seen."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**next step?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "wireframe it. get this into a rough layout and see if the flow holds up. cinematic pacing is a great concept, but if users have to wait through slow transitions every time they click, it’ll get old fast. smooth, intentional movement—yes. frustrating lag—no."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}